<p class="crumb"><a href="{{backUrl}}">&larr; Places</a></p>
<h1>Kinds of place</h1>
<p class="hint">A kind decides what gets recorded. A <em>ranch</em> might record whether the beef is
  grass finished and which cuts they sell; a <em>vendor</em> might record what the discount is and
  who to ask for; a <em>venue</em> might record how many fit and whether there is parking. None of
  that belongs in this program, so you declare it here and every address of that kind gets the
  same boxes.</p>
<p class="hint">A kind can name a template, edited under Content, which renders every place of that
  kind. Without one there is a plain built-in page, which is enough to start.</p>
<div class="doing"><a class="btn" href="{{newUrl}}">{{{plusIcon}}}New kind</a><a class="btn secondary" href="{{backUrl}}">Addresses</a></div>
<div class="panel" data-panel="{{panelUrl}}">{{{panel}}}</div>
